  "body": "Fixes #3119\n\nChild of Goal #3118 (acceptance 2). A consumer's outcome on a session whose **last relayed upstream answer was a 429** is stored (`GET` shows it) but counts **no strike**: the gateway owns the 429 first-hand, and the cell cooldown / rail latch is its whole answer. A capacity death is no verdict on the model, cell or harness.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `gateway/src/agent_gateway/store.py`: `session_last_throttled(session_id)`, the latest `requests` row's status is 429 (the ledger already records every relayed answer; checked, not assumed).\n- `gateway/src/agent_gateway/outcomes.py`: `Outcomes.report` skips the strike for a non-`clean` outcome when that holds. The outcome is still stored, replays and conflicts behave as before, and `clean` refutation is untouched.\n- `gateway/specs/endpoints/sessions.md`: the rule beside \"A 429 writes **no** strike\" (acceptance 1), and four rows in §What the store holds.\n- `gateway/tests/test_sessions_outcome.py`: the four rows as `rule(\"GW-SESSIONS-OUTCOME\")` cases, plus `test_clean_after_429_still_refutes`.\n\n## Spec changes\n\nRequirement: `GW-SESSIONS-OUTCOME` (`gateway/specs/endpoints/sessions.md`), world `policy-default`. Judgment rows (⚖):\n\n- \"a consumer outcome after a relayed 429 strikes nothing ⚖\": `upstream-429`, then the consumer reports `unknown`. No counted strike; the outcome is stored.\n- \"a harness that gave up on a 429 strikes nothing ⚖\": `upstream-429`, then `harness-gave-up`. No strike.\n- \"a 429 followed by a 2xx is no capacity death ⚖\": `upstream-429`, `upstream-ok`, then `unknown`. One model-scoped `unknown` strike (the last answer was a 2xx, so the rule does not apply).\n- \"a clean outcome after a 429 still refutes ⚖\": a counted `no-verdict` from an earlier session is refuted by this session's `clean` after a 429.\n\nProse judgments (⚖), each stated in the spec beside the rule:\n- A **judge's** outcome (`wrong-verdict`) is on the verdict, not the ride, so it still counts. Code: `not judge`. **No row covers this path yet.** It is a judgment with no test.\n- A **canary** ride keeps its task strike. GW-CATALOG-OR §The entry canary (operator 2026-10-22) pins that the 429 withholds only the cell's verdict. The existing test `test_strike_after_429_not_the_verdict` asserts this, so the gate exempts canary rides (`not row.canary_provider`). If you want canary rides under the new rule too, that test's pinned row needs an explicit ruling change, which I did not make here.\n\n## Gate: observed\n\nRun in `gateway/` (`PYTHONPATH=src`, the locked venv, `uv.lock` untouched):\n\n- `pytest` (full gateway suite): **950 passed** (2:27).\n- `ruff check src tests scripts`: **All checks passed!**\n- `scripts/spec_gate.py`: **26 requirements, 0 red**, exit 0. `GW-SESSIONS-OUTCOME: 39 rows, 0 not passed`. `GW-CATALOG-OR: 58 rows, 0 not passed`.\n\nPin-vacuity: on the pre-fix `src/` (spec and tests kept), the new rows \"a consumer outcome after a relayed 429 strikes nothing\" and \"a harness that gave up on a 429 strikes nothing\" **fail** (2 failed, 37 passed). The \"2xx\" and \"clean\" rows are guard rows and pass on both trees, as intended.\n\nNote on the spec gate: the first run on this branch was red on many rules' join ratchets. That came from stale Allure results (the gate reads them). Once the ids matched verbatim (including the `⚖`, per the author brief) and pytest ran fresh, it went to 0 red.\n\n## Tier / process notes\n\n- `Touches:` classifies as `machine-merge` (`classify_touches`). `gateway/**` is not named in the path tiers. This is a code change under the gateway island's CI (`gateway-ci`), and I flag it for the reviewer.\n- Python deps: this ride's egress profile is `none` and `UV_DEFAULT_INDEX` is unset. I installed the locked versions from the mirror at `http://192.168.40.34/simple/` with `uv export --frozen` and hash-checked `uv pip install`, not by editing the lock. The exported requirements file lived in `/tmp`, outside the repo.\n- The `pr-gate` run used `UV_DEFAULT_INDEX=http://192.168.40.34/simple/` for uv. The pinned `allure-evidence` wheel (`scripts/lib/snippets.sh`) pulls `svgwrite` from PyPI, and `pypi.org` is egress-blocked on this ride. Without the override the `gateway-evidence` leg failed to fetch it. The gate's own steps were otherwise unchanged.\n- No `devbox.json`/`devbox.lock` changes (restored from base before the commit).\n\n## Out of scope (per the issue)\n\nThe Go headroom poll (#3108), the agent-runtime half (finalize classifying `usage limit exceeded`), and any new outcome class.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n<!-- agent-touches: begin -->\nTouches-escapes: gateway/src/agent_gateway/store.py\n<!-- agent-touches: end -->",
